# item C4 — cmd/swiftc-corpus

## File created
cmd/swiftc-corpus/main.go — CLI tool to manage and check the swiftc symbol corpus

## Flags implemented
- --corpus <path>       path to corpus.txt (default: auto-located via repo root)
- --divergences <path>  path to swiftc-oracle-divergences.txt
- --regenerate          run "make regenerate" in testdata/swiftc dir
- --check               assert committed corpus matches regeneration output (exit 1 on drift)
- --diff <symbol>       print demangle/remangle/oracle output for one symbol
- --feature <NN>        restrict --check/--diff to symbols from src/NN_*.swift

## Build result
  $ go build ./cmd/swiftc-corpus/
  Result: OK — binary built at ./swiftc-corpus (10.4 MB)
  go vet: no issues

## Test run (--diff on one symbol)
  $ ./swiftc-corpus --diff '$s10BasicTypes04makeA0A2AVyF'
  symbol:   $s10BasicTypes04makeA0A2AVyF
  demangle: (demangle error: swift-stable: grammar violation ... at offset 23)
  remangle: (no tree — demangle failed)
  oracle:   BasicTypes.makeBasic() -> BasicTypes.BasicTypes

Note: demangle error is expected — this symbol's return type uses
the AA self-substitution form which is not yet covered in the Stage 1
parser. The oracle output confirms the expected demangled form.

## End-to-end sanity checks
  $ ./swiftc-corpus --diff '$sBf32_'
  demangle: Builtin.FPIEEE32
  remangle: (remangle error: unsupported BuiltinTypeName)  # expected — R1 gap
  oracle:   Builtin.FPIEEE32

  $ ./swiftc-corpus --diff '$s10BasicTypesAAV'
  demangle: BasicTypes.BasicTypes
  remangle: $s10BasicTypes10BasicTypesV                    # AA expanded — correct
  oracle:   BasicTypes.BasicTypes
